<title>SWEDEN: S&amp;P affirms Skandia, Stadshypotek ratings.</title>
<headline>S&amp;P affirms Skandia, Stadshypotek ratings.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. credit rating agency Standard &amp; Poor's on Wednesday affirmed its ratings for Swedish insurer Skandia and mortgage bank Stadshypotek after the announcement of a proposed merger between the two.  </p>
<p>S&amp;P said in a statement the affirmations were based on the potential for an increased presence for the group in the Nordic financial services market, a certain degree of cost saving, and the low level of additional financial risk incurred.</p>
<p>&quot;The positive ratings outlook on Stadshypotek will be reviewed as the strategy and shape of the proposed new group becomes clearer,&quot; it added.</p>
<p>The Swedish government controls a 34 percent stake in Stadshypotek and says it opposes the planned merger that was announced on Monday.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1004</p>
</text>
